{{Quote|They ''should'' have surrendered, but instead they fought back. Suddenly all the relatively new Knights like me, who mistook our overconfidence for foresight, had to figure out what to do next.|Bultar Swan, on the battle in the Petranaki Arena|<ref name="On the Front Lines">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]''</ref>}}
'''Bultar Swan''' was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]] [[Gender|female]] who [[Jedi training|trained]] as [[Jedi Master]] [[Plo Koon]]'s [[Padawan]] before becoming a [[Jedi Knight]]. Not long after she became a Knight, Swan was among a [[Jedi assault team|group]] of 212 [[Jedi]] that Master [[Mace Windu]] led to the [[Petranaki Arena]] on the [[planet]] [[Geonosis]] in order to rescue Jedi Knight [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] from the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] in [[22 BBY]]. Swan expected the Separatists to surrender, but instead they [[First Battle of Geonosis|fought]] back and deployed their [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]].

Swan fought the [[droid]]s back-to-back with fellow Jedi [[Stass Allie]], but the situation turned against the Jedi and soon the pair were surrounded, along with their other surviving allies. [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] then saved the Jedi in the arena when he arrived with [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]]s carrying the [[clone trooper]]s of the new [[Grand Army of the Republic]]. Swan and Allie climbed aboard one of the gunships, which swiftly left the arena and landed in the nearby [[desert]]s. There, the two Jedi charged into battle with more droid forces and helped to ultimately defeat the Separatists.

==Biography==
===Challenges for a new Knight===
{{Quote|I let my saber training take over. Muscles moved by themselves as I unconsciously ran the sweeping and batting exercise that is blaster deflection. My brain, however, was racing at lightspeed. Events moved alarmingly fast, and they weren't moving in our favor.|Bultar Swan, on the battle in the Petranaki Arena|<ref name="On the Front Lines" />}}
[[File:SwanColemanGeonosis-AOTC.png|thumb|left|300px|Bultar Swan was part of the assault team that traveled to Geonosis to rescue Obi-Wan Kenobi.]]
Bultar Swan was a [[Force-sensitive]] [[human]]<ref name="Force Collection" /> [[Gender|female]]<ref name="Topps" /> who served in the [[Jedi Order]]<ref name="Force Collection" /> as the [[Padawan]] of [[Jedi High Council]] member [[Jedi Master|Master]] [[Plo Koon]],<ref name="2nd Grade Reading" /> who taught her well.<ref name="Pocket" /> At one point the pair discussed the weather.<ref name="2nd Grade Reading" /> By [[22 BBY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: On the Front Lines]]'' states that Bultar Swan was new to being a [[Jedi Knight]] during the [[First Battle of Geonosis]], which ''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates to [[22 BBY]].</ref> Swan had recently ascended to the rank of [[Jedi Knight]] and was among<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> the 212 [[Jedi]]<ref name="UVD">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref> that Master [[Mace Windu]] hastily assembled into an [[Jedi assault team|assault team]] that traveled to the [[planet]] [[Geonosis]] in order to rescue the Jedi Knight [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]].<ref name="AOTC" />

Kenobi had been captured after discovering a secret [[Separatist Droid Army|droid army]] being built by the newly formed [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], and had been taken to the [[Geonosian]]<ref name="AOTC" /> [[Petranaki Arena]]<ref name="Encyclopedia">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia: The Comprehensive Guide to the Star Wars Galaxy]]''</ref> to be [[Death|executed]] alongside his Padawan [[Anakin Skywalker]] and [[Senator]] [[Padmé Amidala Naberrie|Padmé Amidala]], who had been captured during their own attempt to rescue Kenobi. The trio of captives fought off beasts, Geonosians, and [[droid]]s while Swan and her colleagues infiltrated the arena before revealing themselves, [[lightsaber]]s drawn. Swan stood with<ref name="AOTC" /> Jedi Master [[Coleman Trebor]]<ref name="Encyclopedia" /> in the arena stands<ref name="AOTC" /> and expected the Separatists to surrender;<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> however, the Jedi's foes instead deployed their droid army to the arena and fierce [[First Battle of Geonosis|fighting]] broke out between the two factions.<ref name="AOTC" />

===Back to back===
{{Quote|What I saw was bigger than anything I had imagined. Distant rectangles bobbed up and down as they marched in our direction, each speck in the formation representing an armed battle droid. Hoop-wheeled tanks roared past the droids, stirring up clouds of red dust.|Bultar Swan, on the Battle of Geonosis|<ref name="On the Front Lines" />}}
Allowing her [[Jedi training|lightsaber training]] to take over, Swan began unconsciously running through the sweeping and batting exercise of [[blaster]] deflection. For most of the battle she fought back-to-back with fellow Jedi [[Stass Allie]],<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> but the odds eventually turned against the Jedi, with Swan, Allie, and other survivors being forced into a circle on the arena grounds and surrounded by droids. The fighting ceased, and [[Count]] [[Dooku]], [[Head of State|leader]] of the Confederacy, offered Windu the chance for the Jedi to surrender. After the Jedi refused, Dooku ordered his forces to kill Swan and the others.<ref name="AOTC" /> Still beside Allie, Swan sliced through a [[B2-series super battle droid]], and then looked up to see Jedi [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]] on a [[Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry]] [[gunship]].<ref name="On the Front Lines" />

[[File:JediCircle.jpg|thumb|300px|Bultar Swan (center) was among the final surviving Jedi in the arena on Geonosis.]]
Yoda had arrived to rescue the Jedi with the [[clone trooper]]s of the new [[Grand Army of the Republic]],<ref name="AOTC" /> and Swan and Allie leapt together onto the deck of one the other gunships that had arrived in the arena. The pair hung on tightly as the [[Starship|ship]] took off and cleared the arena walls before making a fast landing on the [[desert]] plains outside the arena. Swan could see the distant shapes of Separatist [[battle droid]]s and [[IG-227 Hailfire-class droid tank|IG-227 ''Hailfire''-class droid tanks]] marching toward her, while the [[Galactic Republic]] deployed various war machines that she did not recognize among the many [[Cloning|clone]] [[trooper]]s around her. The new Jedi Knight then shared a nod with Allie, before the pair raised their lightsabers and charged into battle.<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> Ultimately the Republic claimed victory on Geonosis, forcing the surviving Separatists to flee.<ref name="AOTC" /> Swan survived the battle<ref name="Pocket" /> and later gave an account of her actions there.<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> She would go on to become a veteran of the [[Clone Wars]] between the Republic and the Separatists,<ref name="Force Collection">{{ForceCollection|Bultar Swan|star=3}}</ref> which began with the battle on Geonosis.<ref name="AOTC" />

==Personality and traits==
{{Quote|The battle wasn't supposed to happen. I knew it ''might'' happen, but when you're a Jedi, you get accustomed to surrenders as soon as you ignite your lightsaber. And in my defense, we had more than two hundred lightsabers packed into that arena, with Master Windu's only a centimeter from Dooku's throat.|Bultar Swan, on the Battle of Geonosis|<ref name="On the Front Lines" />}}
[[File:FrontLines-BultarSwanFights.png|thumb|left|300px|Bultar Swan (right) fought alongside Stass Allie during the Battle of Geonosis.]]
By the [[time]] she traveled to Geonosis, Swan had grown accustomed to opponents surrendering as soon as a Jedi ignited their lightsaber, and so expected that the Separatists would do the same when more than two hundred members of the Order confronted them. She understood that the battle might happen, but believed it would not until the Separatists fought back, at which point she realized that what she had believed to be foresight on her part had in fact been overconfidence.<ref name="On the Front Lines" />

While her muscles moved unconsciously to deflect incoming bolts, her mind was racing as the events around her unfolded quickly, forcing her focus to narrow down to only herself and her moment-to-moment survival. When she spotted Yoda during the fighting, her first thought was only to wonder how long had he been present. The larger-scale conflict on the desert plains was bigger then anything Swan had ever imagined, and as she engaged she realized that what she was seeing was a full-scale war.<ref name="On the Front Lines" /> The Jedi Knight fought courageously on Geonosis, which marked the beginning of her boldest adventures in the field.<ref name="Topps" /> Swan had [[Color|black]] [[hair]], tan skin, and brown [[eye]]s.<ref name="AOTC" /> She stood 1.68 [[meter]]s (5 [[foot]], 5 inches) tall.<ref name="Pocket" />

==Powers and abilities==
Bultar Swan was known for her ability to defeat her enemies using non-lethal methods. Her knowledge of [[Unarmed combat|martial arts]] led to a new form of combat that combined physical attacks with using a lightsaber for defense.<ref name="Force Collection" />

==Equipment==
{{Quote|So this was what war looked like. Stass and I shared a nod, raised our lightsabers, and charged.|Bultar Swan, on the Battle of Geonosis|<ref name="On the Front Lines" />}}
While on Geonosis, Bultar Swan wore a set of light and dark brown [[Jedi apparel|Jedi robes]] with the darker elements including a [[Clothing|tunic]], [[boot]]s, and pants. She used a green-bladed [[Bultar Swan's lightsaber|lightsaber]] with a silver colored hilt.<ref name="AOTC" />

==Behind the scenes==
===''Attack of the Clones''===
{{Quote|⭐️Wars Bultar Swan - another Ep2 sketch that evolved in to a character. Slide right for the less Jedi version|Dermot Power|<ref name="IG">{{Instagram|username=powerdermot|name=[[Dermot Power]]|url=p/CO4p_phDWE_|date=2021-05-15|quote=⭐️Wars Bultar Swan - another Ep2 sketch that evolved in to a character. Slide right for the less Jedi version|archivefile=File:BultarSwan-DermotPower-Instagram.png}}</ref>}}
[[File:Bultarconceptart.jpg|thumb|right|300px|Concept art of Bultar Swan, production code dp383b]]
Bultar Swan was portrayed by actress [[Mimi Daraphet]]<ref name="databank">{{DB|character|bultarswan|Swan, Bultar}}</ref> in the [[prequel trilogy]] film [[Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones|''Star Wars'': Episode II ''Attack of the Clones'']],<ref name="AOTC" /> which was released on [[May 16]], [[2002]].<ref name="Year by Year">''[[Star Wars Year By Year: A Visual History, New Edition]]''</ref> Prior to the release of the film, Swan was shown in the trailer for Episode II<ref name="Trailer">{{SW|url=video/episode-ii-trailer-clone-war|text=Attack of the Clones Trailer: Clone War &#124; Video}}</ref> released on [[March 10]], 2002.<ref name="TrailerRelease">{{WebCite|url=https://ew.com/article/2002/03/04/sneak-peek-next-episode-ii-trailer|text=A sneak peek at the next <nowiki>''</nowiki>Episode II<nowiki>''</nowiki> trailer|author=Brown, Scott|date=2002-03-04|quote=On March 10, the latest two-and-a-half-minute tease for "Attack of the Clones" will hit screens|archivedate=20231127115801}}</ref> Daraphet was cast by extra casting director [[Ros Breden]]<ref name="oldswcom">{{SWArchive|url=episode-ii/bts/profile/f20020131/index.html|text=Extras, Extras: Ros Breden}}</ref> but the character started out as a concept sketch. At least two pieces of concept art of the character were created by [[Dermot Power]] in [[June]], [[2000]], with the production codes  "dp383" and "dp383b." The former was a "less Jedi version" depicting the character wearing white and gray robes and with her hair fastened up in a braid.<ref name="IG" /> Her outfit in Episode II is very similar to the leather-accented ensemble worn by Anakin Skywalker in the film.<ref name="databank" /> The Jedi battle in the Geonosis arena scenes were filmed on Stage 3 at [[Fox Studios, Sydney]], between [[August 10]] and [[August 15]], 2000.<ref name="Archives">''[[The Star Wars Archives: Episodes I–III, 1999–2005]]''</ref>

The character was revealed to the public prior to the release of the Episode II, when a publicity still of Swan debuted on [[StarWars.com]] on [[January 31]], 2002, captioned "Bultar Swan, heroic Jedi."<ref name="oldswcom" /> In the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], Bultar Swan's name was first used in the [[Star Wars video games|mobile card game]] ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'',<ref name="Force Collection" /> which initially launched in [[2013]]. Although the launch of ''Force Collection'' predates<ref name="Force Collection release">{{SW|url=news/announcing-star-wars-force-collection|text=Announcing Star Wars: Force Collection|nolive=1}}</ref> the ''Star Wars'' canon reset of [[2014]],<ref name="Legends">{{SW|url=news/the-legendary-star-wars-expanded-universe-turns-a-new-page|text=The Legendary Star Wars Expanded Universe Turns a New Page}}</ref> [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Leland Chee]] confirmed that the game was kept updated to fit with canon.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|holocronkeeper|status/846807700482666496|[[Leland Chee]]|quote=I'm not gonna go through the trouble of changing them and I don't have any reason to believe currently that anyone would. [&hellip;] On the off-chance that we DID have a current need to change any of these, we would have for Force Collection.|archivedate=20210505080831}} &mdash; [[Leland Chee]] of the [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] has confirmed that [[in-universe]] information from ''[[Star Wars: Force Collection]]'' conforms with ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]].</ref>

===''Revenge of the Sith''===
[[File:DermotPower-BultarSwanLessJedi-Instagram.jpg|thumb|left|300px|alt=A sketch of a "less Jedi" version of Bultar Swan shows her in white and gray robes with her hair fastened up in a braid, but still carrying a lightsaber on her belt.|Dermot Power created a "less-Jedi" concept of Bultar Swan.]]
Extras Casting for the [[2005]] film [[Star Wars: Episode III Revenge of the Sith|''Star Wars'': Episode III ''Revenge of the Sith'']] managed to track down Daraphet and several other actors who had appeared in the previous films<ref name="Separatists & Swan">{{Hyperspace|url=hyperspace/member/episode-iii/bts/setdiary/news20050605.html|series=Episode III Set Diary|text=Separatists & Swan}}</ref><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress">{{WordPress|subdomain=swhyperspace|url=episode-iii/set-diary/|name=SW Hyperspace|text=Set Diary|archivedate=20251223144913}}</ref> and although Swan did not yet appear in the shooting script, which was still being finalized at the time, there was enough Jedi action scenes that it was deemed prudent preparation to call her in for a fitting.<ref name="Jedi Missing in Action">{{Hyperspace|url=hyperspace/member/episode-iii/bts/setdiary/news20050627.html|series=Episode III Set Diary|text=Jedi Missing In Action}}</ref><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" /> Initially it was thought Daraphet would not be able to return as her agency stated that she was in [[Wikipedia:Hong Kong|Hong Kong]]; however, it turned out that she had simply stopped using the agency.<ref name="Separatists & Swan" /><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" />

On [[June 5]], [[2003]], three days after she got a call about being in the film, she was fitted for a short wig in hair and makeup by Key Hairdresser [[Annette Miles]]<ref name="Separatists & Swan" /><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" /> back at Fox Studios, [[Wikipedia:Sydney|Sydney]].<ref name="Jedi Missing in Action" /><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" /> During the fitting she spoke with [[Pablo Hidalgo]], author of the film's [[Episode III Set Diary|Set Diary]], and then headed to costumes to test out a Jedi outfit for Episode III. Daraphet was excited to get the call to be in Episode III, as she had thought she would not be in the film given that Swan might had died during the last fight scene of ''Attack of the Clones''.<ref name="Separatists & Swan" /><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" /> Once the shooting schedule arrived it became clear that most of the material being shot for [[Order 66]] scenes would happen during pickup photography rather than principal photography and so testing for Swan had been premature.<ref name="Jedi Missing in Action" /><ref name="Hyperspace Wordpress" /> Ultimately the character did not appear in the film.<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref>

